  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is the current best at 0.678 acc / 0.646 F1, showing that scvi_n200 substantially outperforms pca_n2000 (+0.039) in the multimodal setting. With pca_n2000, resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l were nearly equivalent (0.639 vs 0.635), so the image-encoder choice was not clearly resolved. Question: Does the stronger, learned scvi_n200 RNA representation change the relative value of the image encoder, potentially allowing the larger ViT-L to contribute more complementary spatial/visual features than ResNet50? Why this experiment: It is the most direct single-variable extension of the best-known configuration (only image encoder changes from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l), maximizing the chance of incremental improvement while also resolving whether the image-encoder choice is truly negligible or becomes relevant when paired with a richer RNA embedding. Under a limited budget, exploiting the strongest identified direction with a minimal, well-motivated perturbation is the highest-expected-value next step."
}

